### 3.5 Write Verification Protocol

#### Level 1: Size Check (Minimum Requirement)
```bash
TARGET="/mnt/user/platinum_admin/logs/output.log"
echo "data" > "$TARGET"

if [ -s "$TARGET" ]; then
    log_info "Write successful: $TARGET ($(stat -c%s "$TARGET") bytes)"
else
    log_err "Write failed: $TARGET is empty or missing"
    exit 1
fi
```

#### Level 2: Content Validation (Recommended for Configs)
```bash
EXPECTED_PATTERN="server_name.*example.com"
if grep -q "$EXPECTED_PATTERN" "$TARGET"; then
    log_info "Config validation passed"
else
    log_err "Config missing required pattern: $EXPECTED_PATTERN"
    exit 1
fi
```

#### Level 3: Checksum Verification (Critical Files)
```bash
EXPECTED_SHA256="a3b5c8d9..."  # Pre-computed hash
ACTUAL_SHA256=$(sha256sum "$TARGET" | awk '{print $1}')

if [ "$ACTUAL_SHA256" = "$EXPECTED_SHA256" ]; then
    log_info "Checksum verified"
else
    log_err "Checksum mismatch! File may be corrupted"
    exit 1
fi
```

